<!--
  Every <info> block ended, which is what ECCC sends when an alert finishes for
  the whole region: msgType stays "Update" (never "Cancel"), and each block
  keeps an hour of <expires> on the clock. Without the Alert_Location_Status
  rule this document builds a live entity whose headline reads "…- ended" and
  which survives until that expiry — defect B of issue #45, in isolation.

  Timestamps are pinned to 2099 for the reason given in
  eccc_cap_mixed_area_groups.xml: the wall clock must not be what retires this
  alert, or the test proves nothing about the lifecycle parameter.
-->
